      "created_at": "2026-08-30T16:09:28Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-08-30T16:09:28Z",
      "body": "Thank you very much for releasing MAP, the pretrained weights, and the accompanying code. We are trying to perform an inference-only reproduction of the Tahoe-100M unprofiled-drug evaluation using the released `epoch_3.pt`, without any retraining or fine-tuning.\n\nTo reproduce the reported all-HVG and top-50 DEG Pearson delta correlations exactly, could you kindly share the following artifacts, if available?\n\n1. The exact ordered 2,000-HVG gene list used by `epoch_3.pt`.\n2. The evaluation split files, particularly `external_test_indices.json` and `control_indices.json`, together with the final 16 held-out drug identifiers and evaluation random seeds.\n3. A source commit or minimal inference script that is fully compatible with the released checkpoint.\n4. The metric implementation or precise settings for:\n   - all-HVG Pearson delta correlation;\n   - top-50 DEG Pearson delta correlation, including how the top 50 genes were selected;\n   - aggregation across the five pseudobulk evaluations.\n\nIf it is easier, saved predicted, observed and matched-control pseudobulk matrices would also be sufficient for us to verify the published delta correlations and calculate an additional delta-expression R\u00b2.\n\nWe greatly appreciate your work and understand that preparing reproducibility materials takes additional effort. These small artifacts would make the released checkpoint independently evaluable without requiring retraining or reconstruction of the full Tahoe dataset.\n\nThank you very much for your time and help!",
      "author_association": "NONE",
      "pin": null,
